Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: nekobox
Source: https://github.com/qr243vbi/nekobox
Comment: Scope and evidence.
 .
 This file covers the material that is compiled into the two programs in
 the binary package (the Qt GUI nekobox and the Go core nekobox_core) and
 the third-party material that those programs embed. It is not a full
 audit of every file in the source tarball.
 .
 Licence and notice files that upstream ships are copied verbatim by
 scripts/collect-notices.py into debian/third-party/ and installed under
 /usr/share/doc/nekobox/third-party/. INDEX.txt maps every copied file to
 its source path and sha256. Inline notices that have no separate file are
 copied to the same place under generated/inline/.
 .
 The release tarball does not ship a licence file for a few components.
 For those, debian/third-party/upstream/PROVENANCE.txt records the project,
 the retrieval date and, where possible, a byte-for-byte match between the
 vendored source and the upstream file. Files whose origin could not be
 established are marked "unresolved" below rather than guessed.
 .
 dh_compress gzip-compresses files under /usr/share/doc that are larger
 than 4 KiB, so a text named below as ".../LICENSE" may be installed as
 ".../LICENSE.gz". INDEX.txt records the uncompressed names.
 .
 Parts of the source tarball that this package does not compile are not
 itemised here: core/updater/ (SKIP_UPDATER=ON; no updater executable is
 installed), src/3rdparty/lmdbxx/ (MIGRATE_LMDB=OFF) and the test suites
 (except cpr/test, noted below because its licence differs from cpr's root
 licence). They are not in the binary package.
 .
 The Go runtime and standard library are statically linked into
 nekobox_core by the golang-1.26-go build dependency. Their source is not
 part of the upstream tarball and is not copied here; on the build system
 see /usr/share/doc/golang-1.26-go/copyright (BSD-3-clause, Copyright
 2009 The Go Authors).
 .
 The GUI links system libraries dynamically (Qt6, Boost, OpenSSL, curl,
 leveldb, thrift, yaml-cpp, snappy, acl, X11/XCB). They are not bundled and
 are covered by their own Debian packages.
 .
 res/fonts/NotoEmoji.ttf and res/fonts/TwemojiCOLR.ttf are present in the
 source tree but are NOT embedded in this build: on non-Windows CMake sets
 ENABLE_EMOJI_EMBEEDING=OFF, and the GUI binary contains only the fallback
 path strings, not the font data. Their licences are therefore not part of
 the binary package. See upstream/PROVENANCE.txt before enabling that
 option.

