 and sha256 is in debian/third-party/INDEX.txt.

Files: debian/third-party/README
       debian/third-party/INDEX.txt
       debian/third-party/upstream/PROVENANCE.txt
Copyright: 2026 Oblivion W <oblivion.w23@gmail.com>
License: GPL-3
Comment: Packaging documentation about the copied texts, not a copied text.

Files: core/server/vendor/*
Copyright: the respective module authors, as stated in each module's licence files
License: per-module
Comment: The complete licence and notice files of every module in the
 vendored build set are installed as
 /usr/share/doc/nekobox/third-party/generated/go/<module>/ and indexed in
 INDEX.txt. They are copied verbatim, not summarised or relicensed here.
 .
 The set comes from core/server/vendor/modules.txt. It is a superset of the
 modules actually linked into the amd64 core binary (for example,
 Windows-only modules are vendored but not linked), so some copied licences
 belong to modules that contribute no code to this binary. The 112 modules
 reported as dependencies by the built core all have at least one copied
 licence file; the copies are kept for the whole vendor set so that the
 inventory can be regenerated from the source tree alone.

Files: src/3rdparty/cpr/*
Copyright: 2017-2021 Huu Nguyen; 2022 libcpr and many other contributors
License: MIT
Comment: Bundled cpr is always used (CMAKE_DISABLE_FIND_PACKAGE_cpr=ON) and
 is statically linked into the GUI; libcurl itself is a system library.
 Complete text: /usr/share/doc/nekobox/third-party/generated/cpp/cpr/LICENSE.

